            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to quake, then the Hindi for a shock (of grief or fright)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पीटना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पीटना — pīṭnā — \"to beat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दो आदमियों ने एक चोर को पीटा। do ādmiyoṁ ne ek cor ko pīṭā. Two men beat up a thief."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने ढोल पीटा, usne ḍhol pīṭā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "goes back to Sanskrit piṭṭayati, to pound into a flat mass, beside which CDIAL reconstructs piṭṭyatē, \"is struck\" (CDIAL 8165). It is hitting again and again; you also पीटना (pīṭnā) a drum: ढोल पीटना (pīṭnā)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
